   "text": "I read the drawing as a cyclic peptide-like macrocycle and traced it residue by residue, starting from the 7-membered lactam.\n\n**Residues in order around the ring**\n1. A caprolactam (azepan-2-one) ring: N1, C2(=O), C3 (bearing N-methyl, wedged ring CH2), two CH2 groups, CH(CH3) with a wedged methyl, and a CH2 back to N1.\n2. From C3: N(Me)\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2 (a sarcosine unit), then N(Me)\u2013C(=O) leading to an isoleucine \u03b1-carbon.\n3. Isoleucine, with the sec-butyl side chain, then NH\u2013C(=O) to a cyclopropylalanine \u03b1-carbon with its N-methyl.\n4. N(Me)\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2 to an aspartic-type \u03b1-carbon whose side-chain carbonyl is a morpholine amide, then its N-methyl.\n5. N(Me)\u2013C(=O) to a cyclopentylglycine \u03b1-carbon with its N-methyl.\n6. N(Me)\u2013C(=O) to a 1-aminocyclobutane-1-carboxamide (no stereocentre), then NH\u2013C(=O) to proline.\n7. The proline nitrogen acylated by a homophenylalanine \u03b1-carbon whose aryl group is 3-chloro-4-CF3-phenyl. The aryl ring is attached at one carbon, with CF3 para and Cl meta to the attachment point.\n8. That residue's NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013N(Me)\u2013C(=O) leads to the \u03b1-carbon bearing a CH2\u2013(4-CF3-phenyl) group, which closes onto the lactam N1.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each wedge or hash by CIP priorities and converted to @/@@ for the SMILES neighbour order. The results:\n- Lactam C3: S.\n- Lactam CH(CH3): R.\n- \u03b1-carbon bearing the 4-CF3-benzyl group: R.\n- Isoleucine \u03b1: S; isoleucine \u03b2: S.\n- Cyclopropylalanine \u03b1: S.\n- Aspartate-type \u03b1: S.\n- Cyclopentylglycine \u03b1: S.\n- Proline \u03b1: S.\n- Homophenylalanine \u03b1: S.\n\nI checked ring closures and branch order by hand but did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\nSMILES: O=C1N2C[C@H](C)CC[C@@H]1N(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)CC)NC(=O)[C@H](CC3CC3)N(C)C(=O)C[C@@H](C(=O)N4CCOCC4)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](C5CCCC5)N(C)C(=O)C6(CCC6)NC(=O)[C@@H]7CCCN7C(=O)[C@H](CCc8ccc(C(F)(F